Under tab-size: 0, Ladybird gives each preserved tab no advance. In
Chrome 157.0.8103.79, Firefox 151.0, and WebKit 26.5, an X after “a” and
two tabs sits right after the a, at one character’s advance. WebKit’s
FontCascade::tabWidth() and Blink’s Font::TabWidth() return the letter
spacing for a tab size of 0 rather than dividing by it.
